'''BSE Limited''', also known as the '''Bombay Stock Exchange''' ('''BSE'''), is an Indian [[stock exchange]] based in [[Mumbai]]. Established in 1875, it is the oldest stock exchange in Asia, and also the tenth oldest in the world. It is the [[List of stock exchanges|6th largest stock exchange]] in the world by total [[market capitalisation]], exceeding $5 trillion in May 2024.<ref name="WFE">{{cite web|url=https://www.world-exchanges.org/home/index.php/monthly-reports-tool|title=Monthly Reports - World Federation of Exchanges|publisher=WFE|access-date=21 May 2018|archive-date=11 January 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230111193701/https://www.world-exchanges.org/our-work/statistics|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="bseindia.com">{{cite web |title=BSE-Introduction |url=http://www.bseindia.com/static/about/introduction.aspx?expandable=0 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180131201340/http://www.bseindia.com/static/about/introduction.aspx?expandable=0 |archive-date=31 January 2018 |access-date=31 January 2018 |website=bseindia.com}}</ref><ref name="Rawal2015">{{cite book |author=Priya Rawal |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=xLsoCAAAQBAJ&pg=PA12 |title=Indian Stock Market and Investors Strategy |date=16 April 2015 |publisher=Priya Rawal |isbn=978-1-5053-5668-7 |pages=12– |access-date=23 November 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230111193659/https://books.google.com/books?id=xLsoCAAAQBAJ&pg=PA12 |archive-date=11 January 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=10 September 2020 |title=10 Oldest Stock Exchanges in the World |url=https://www.oldest.org/technology/stock-exchanges/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210304212435/https://www.oldest.org/technology/stock-exchanges/ |archive-date=4 March 2021}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:Bombay Stock Exchange logo.svg|thumb|Bombay Stock Exchange logo used until June 2023]] 
Bombay Stock Exchange was founded by a [[Jain]] businessman [[Premchand Roychand]] in 1875.<ref>{{cite news |title=BSE may set another record, become an official tourist spot |url=https://www.newindianexpress.com/cities/mumbai/2017/oct/06/bse-may-set-another-record-become-an-official-tourist-spot-1667426.html |access-date=4 November 2021 |work=[[The New Indian Express]] |agency=[[Press Trust of India]] |date=6 October 2017 |archive-date=4 November 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211104151832/https://www.newindianexpress.com/cities/mumbai/2017/oct/06/bse-may-set-another-record-become-an-official-tourist-spot-1667426.html |url-status=live }}</ref> While BSE Limited is now synonymous with [[Dalal Street]], it was not always so. In the 1850s, four [[Gujarati people|Gujarati]] and one [[Parsis|Parsi]] stockbroker gathered together under a [[banyan]] tree in front of Bombay (now Mumbai) Town Hall, where Horniman Circle is now situated.<ref name="bseindia.com" /><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/289504506|title=The Profile of the Bombay Stock Exchange Limited}}</ref> A decade later, the brokers moved their location to under the banyan trees at the junction of Meadows Street and what was then called Esplanade Road, now MG Road. With a rapid increase in the number of brokers, they had to shift places repeatedly. At last, in 1874, the brokers found a permanent location, the one that they could call their own. The brokers group became an official organisation known as "The Native Share & Stock Brokers Association" in 1875.<ref>{{cite web |title=The History of Bombay Stock Exchange | date=11 September 2014 | via=[[YouTube]] |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oDkiJcRWvRQ| archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/varchive/youtube/20211030/oDkiJcRWvRQ| archive-date=2021-10-30}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

In 1957, the BSE became the first stock exchange to be recognised by the [[Second Nehru ministry|Indian Government]] under the Securities Contracts Regulation Act.<ref name="q723">{{cite book | last=Pradhan | first=Rudra Prakash | title=Forecasting Financial Markets in India | publisher=Allied Publishers | date=2009 | isbn=978-81-8424-426-7 | url=https://books.google.com/books?id=D_8eoSMaD8cC&pg=PA54&dq | page=54}}</ref>

The BSE is also a Partner Exchange of the [[Sustainable Stock Exchanges Initiative|United Nations Sustainable Stock Exchange initiative]], joining in September 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) commits to promoting sustainability|url=http://unctad.org/en/pages/newsdetails.aspx?OriginalVersionID=310&Sitemap_x0020_Taxonomy=ISAR%20-%20Corporate%20Transparency%20-%20Accounting;#6;|work=UNCTAD| date=28 September 2012 |access-date=2016-04-29|archive-date=2 April 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150402104057/http://unctad.org/en/pages/newsdetails.aspx?OriginalVersionID=310&Sitemap_x0020_Taxonomy=ISAR%20-%20Corporate%20Transparency%20-%20Accounting;#6;|url-status=live}}</ref> 

BSE established the [[India International Exchange]] (India INX) on 30th December 2016. India INX, based out of [[GIFT City]], is the first international stock exchange of India.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.indiainx.com/static/about.aspx|title=India INX|website=indiainx.com|access-date=15 March 2018|archive-date=18 October 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181018051133/http://www.indiainx.com/static/about.aspx|url-status=live}}</ref> 

BSE became the first stock exchange in the country to launch commodity derivatives contract in gold and silver in October 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/bse-launches-commodity-derivative-contracts-in-gold-silver/article25095987.ece|title=India thehindubusinessline|website=Business Line|date=October 2018 |access-date=25 October 2018|archive-date=27 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200727013230/https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/bse-launches-commodity-derivative-contracts-in-gold-silver/article25095987.ece|url-status=live}}</ref> 

BSE was [[demutualised]] and corporatised on 19 May 2007, pursuant to the ''BSE (Corporatisation and Demutualisation) Scheme, 2005'' notified by [[Securities and Exchange Board of India|SEBI]].<ref>{{cite news |title=BSE demutualisation complete |newspaper=Business Standard India |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/markets/bse-demutualisation-complete-107051901004_1.html |access-date=27 November 2022 |date=14 June 2013 |archive-date=27 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221127070222/https://www.business-standard.com/article/markets/bse-demutualisation-complete-107051901004_1.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Order in respect of BSE (Corporatisation and Demutualisation) Scheme, 2005 |url=https://www.sebi.gov.in/enforcement/orders/may-2005/order-in-respect-of-bse-corporatisation-and-demutualisation-scheme-2005_10748.html |website=sebi.gov.in |access-date=27 November 2022 |archive-date=27 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221127070229/https://www.sebi.gov.in/enforcement/orders/may-2005/order-in-respect-of-bse-corporatisation-and-demutualisation-scheme-2005_10748.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

BSE Limited listed on the [[National Stock Exchange of India|National Stock Exchange]] (NSE) on 3 February 2017 under the [[ticker symbol]] of "BSE".<ref>{{cite web |title=BSE to list on NSE on 3 February |url=https://www.livemint.com/Money/YkU9l96zXEAC2FiRGXZpYJ/BSE-to-list-on-NSE-on-3-February.html |website=Livemint |access-date=27 November 2022 |date=29 January 2017 |archive-date=27 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221127070222/https://www.livemint.com/Money/YkU9l96zXEAC2FiRGXZpYJ/BSE-to-list-on-NSE-on-3-February.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author1=Manu Balachandran |title=142 years after taking roots under a banyan, Asia's oldest stock exchange hits the capital market today |url=https://qz.com/india/886214/bse-ipo-142-years-after-taking-roots-under-a-banyan-asias-oldest-stock-exchange-hits-the-capital-market-today |work=[[Quartz (publication)|Quartz]]|access-date=27 November 2022 |date=22 January 2017 |archive-date=27 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221127070222/https://qz.com/india/886214/bse-ipo-142-years-after-taking-roots-under-a-banyan-asias-oldest-stock-exchange-hits-the-capital-market-today |url-status=live }}</ref>{{efn-la|SEBI Regulation 45(1) of Securities Contracts (Regulation) (Stock Exchanges and Clearing Corporations) Regulations, 2018 prohibits self-listing of a stock exchange in India.<ref>{{cite web |title=Securities Contracts (Regulation) (Stock Exchanges and Clearing Corporations) Regulations, 2018 [Last amended on June 04, 2019] |url=https://www.sebi.gov.in/legal/regulations/oct-2018/securities-contracts-regulation-stock-exchanges-and-clearing-corporations-regulations-2018-last-amended-on-june-04-2019-_40623.html |website=sebi.gov.in |access-date=27 November 2022 |archive-date=11 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230111193729/https://www.sebi.gov.in/legal/regulations/oct-2018/securities-contracts-regulation-stock-exchanges-and-clearing-corporations-regulations-2018-last-amended-on-june-04-2019-_40623.html |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

==Criticism and controversies==
[[File:Stamp of India - 2016 - Colnect 627075 - Bombay Stock Exchange.jpeg|thumb|Stamp of India 2016 Bombay Stock Exchange]]
{{See also|1992 Indian stock market scam}} 
BSE has witnessed several high-profile market manipulation scandals.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/how-indias-trading-queen-and-mystery-guru-engulfed-nse-in-scandal/articleshow/90343226.cms?from=mdr | title=How India's trading queen and mystery guru engulfed NSE in scandal | newspaper=The Economic Times }}</ref><ref>{{cite news | url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/the-fall-of-nse-corruption-or-hubris/articleshow/69154289.cms | title=The fall of NSE: Corruption or hubris? | newspaper=The Economic Times | last1=Rangan | first1=MC Govardhana }}</ref><ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.reuters.com/article/idINIndia-53153120101125 | title=BSE Sensex drops as corruption scandal weighs | work=Reuters | date=25 November 2010 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.businesstoday.in/latest/corporate/story/sebi-penalises-bse-nse-for-laxity-in-karvy-fraud-case-329647-2022-04-13 | title=SEBI penalises BSE, NSE for 'laxity' in Karvy fraud case | date=13 April 2022 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/markets/trading-queen-and-mystery-guru-strange-tale-engulfs-nse-in-scandal-122032100123_1.html | title=Trading 'queen' and mystery guru: Strange tale engulfs NSE in scandal | newspaper=Business Standard India | date=21 March 2022 }}</ref> At times, the [[Securities and Exchange Board of India]] (SEBI) has barred several individuals and entities from trading on the exchanges for [[insider trading]] and [[Market manipulation|stock manipulation]], especially in [[Market liquidity|illiquid]] [[small cap company|small-caps]] and [[penny stocks]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Sreedhar |first1=Vidya |title=Rs 144 crore wrongful profit! Sebi finds stock manipulation in 5 smallcaps |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-bars-135-entities-from-market-on-alleged-share-manipulation-in-5-smallcaps/articleshow/101167757.cms |website=The Economic Times |access-date=24 August 2023 |date=21 June 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Sebi ban pinches penny stocks |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/markets/sebi-ban-pinches-penny-stocks-105102601049_1.html |access-date=24 August 2023 |work=Business Standard}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=SEBI Cracks Down on Misuse of Penny Stocks |url=https://thewire.in/business/penny-stocks-bogus-claims-sebi |access-date=24 August 2023 |work=The Wire}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=I-T Department, SEBI begin crackdown on penny stock firms in PMO-led push |url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/markets/i-t-department-sebi-begin-crackdown-on-penny-stock-firms-in-pmo-led-push-2442315.html |access-date=24 August 2023 |work=Moneycontrol |date=20 November 2017 |language=en}}</ref>

The BSE faced criticism during the early 2000s for delayed technology upgrades, which contributed to its competitor NSE gaining market dominance in [[electronic trading]]. In 2013, market participants raised concerns over alleged preferential access to BSE's trading systems, prompting calls for improved transparency and oversight, though no regulatory action followed.<ref>{{cite news |title=Preferential access? A look into how NSE got ahead in tech race |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/markets/preferential-access-a-look-into-how-nse-got-ahead-in-tech-race-117021000058_1.html |work=Business Standard |date=10 February 2017 |access-date=14 June 2025}}</ref>

